### MojoPay Omni integration — manual request book
### Requires VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
### Fill in the variables below, then run each request with "Send Request".

@baseUrl = https://omni.mojo-pay.com/v1
@clientId = your-client-id
@clientSecret = your-client-secret

# After running "Get token" below, paste the returned access_token here.
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

@mobile = 233XXXXXXXXX
@provider = MTN
@merchantRef = TEST-{{$timestamp}}


### ============================================================
### 1. Auth
### ============================================================

### Get token
# @name getToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_id": "{{clientId}}",
  "client_secret": "{{clientSecret}}"
}


### ============================================================
### 2. Collections
### ============================================================

### Create collection (fixed amount, small test value)
# @name createCollection
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "currency": "GHS",
  "amount": "0.50",
  "merchant_reference": "{{merchantRef}}",
  "description": "Omni smoke test",
  "mobile": "{{mobile}}",
  "provider": "{{provider}}"
}

### Get collection by id (replace CL_... with id from createCollection response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/collections/CL_REPLACE_ME
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### 3. Hosted checkout
### ============================================================

### Create checkout session — fixed amount
# @name createCheckout
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkout/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "amount_mode": "fixed",
  "currency": "GHS",
  "amount": "0.50",
  "merchant_reference": "{{merchantRef}}",
  "description": "Omni checkout smoke test",
  "success_url": "https://example.com/paid",
  "cancel_url": "https://example.com/cancelled"
}

### Create checkout session — open amount (rejected while in Testing mode)
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkout/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "amount_mode": "open",
  "currency": "GHS",
  "merchant_reference": "{{merchantRef}}",
  "description": "Open amount session",
  "success_url": "https://example.com/paid",
  "cancel_url": "https://example.com/cancelled"
}


### ============================================================
### 4. Verify by merchant reference
### ============================================================

### Unified verify — replace TEST-... with a real merchant_reference
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/verify/TEST-REPLACE_ME
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### 5. Payouts
### ============================================================

### Mobile money payout
POST {{baseUrl}}/payouts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "type": "mobile_money",
  "currency": "GHS",
  "amount": "0.50",
  "merchant_reference": "{{merchantRef}}",
  "mobile": "{{mobile}}",
  "provider": "{{provider}}",
  "narration": "Omni payout smoke test"
}

### Get payout status
GET {{baseUrl}}/payouts/TEST-REPLACE_ME
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### 6. Verifications
### ============================================================

### Verify mobile (MSISDN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/verifications/msisdn
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mobile": "{{mobile}}",
  "provider": "{{provider}}"
}

### Verify bank account
POST {{baseUrl}}/verifications/bank_accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bank_code": "300304",
  "account_number": "REPLACE_ACCOUNT_NUMBER"
}


### ============================================================
### 7. Metadata & balance
### ============================================================

### Mobile providers (use these codes for provider field — never hardcode)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata/mobile_providers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Banks
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata/banks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### 8. Account context
### ============================================================

### Confirm which account the token resolves to
GET {{baseUrl}}/account
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### 9. Webhook — simulate a MojoPay delivery (run in terminal)
### ============================================================
# Replace WEBHOOK_URL with your webhook.site URL (https://webhook.site)
# Replace WEBHOOK_SECRET with the secret from the portal.
#
# WEBHOOK_URL="https://webhook.site/your-uuid"
# WEBHOOK_SECRET="whsec_from_portal"
# TIMESTAMP=$(date +%s)
# BODY='{"id":"EVT_TEST001ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQR","type":"collection.succeeded","api_version":"2026-04-15","created":"2026-04-15T10:05:00Z","data":{"object":{"id":"CL_TEST","object":"collection","status":"succeeded","currency":"GHS","amount":"0.50","merchant_reference":"TEST-001","payment_rail":"mobile_money","provider":"MTN"}}}'
# SIG=$(printf '%s' "${TIMESTAMP}.${BODY}" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "${WEBHOOK_SECRET}" | awk '{print $NF}')
# curl -sS -X POST "${WEBHOOK_URL}" \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -H "MojoPay-Signature: t=${TIMESTAMP},v1=${SIG}" \
#   -d "${BODY}"
